From 132ebd37abca97df702039efbdb685f1c41e4b56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shahed <jamshidalinezhadian@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 01:52:00 +0330
Subject: [PATCH] bp1a: let SystemUI draw the navigation bar on phones again

Since QPR2 SystemUI hands the phone navigation bar to whichever launcher
provides recents (TaskbarDelegate) and expects that launcher to draw it.
Trebuchet does, anything else doesn't, so with a ported One UI Home as
the recents provider the 3-button bar was just gone.

Turn enable_taskbar_navbar_unification off so SystemUI draws its own bar
for every launcher again, like before QPR2. Launcher3 checks the same
flag, so Trebuchet stops drawing its copy and there is no double bar.
Large screens still get the taskbar.
---
 .../enable_taskbar_navbar_unification_flag_values.textproto     | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/aconfig/bp1a/com.android.wm.shell/enable_taskbar_navbar_unification_flag_values.textproto b/aconfig/bp1a/com.android.wm.shell/enable_taskbar_navbar_unification_flag_values.textproto
index 7486856..3371a08 100644
--- a/aconfig/bp1a/com.android.wm.shell/enable_taskbar_navbar_unification_flag_values.textproto
+++ b/aconfig/bp1a/com.android.wm.shell/enable_taskbar_navbar_unification_flag_values.textproto
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 flag_value {
   package: "com.android.wm.shell"
   name: "enable_taskbar_navbar_unification"
-  state: ENABLED
+  state: DISABLED
   permission: READ_ONLY
 }
-- 
